research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-geometric-function-taylor-remainder.log-7-BOUNDARY: The public claim holds for all real x ≠ 1; the Taylor polynomial identity extends to x = 1 as well. The exact remainder matches the algebraic identity 1/(1−x) − Σ_{j=0}^n x^j = x^{n+1}/(1−x), requiring no convergence conditions. Standard boundary cases (empty, zero, one, degenerate, endpoints) are inapplicable or satisfied, and the proof does not rely on any hidden choice.
