research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-taylor-remainder-bound.result.json-16-  "tail": "````text\nVERDICT: CLEAN\n```\n\nBOUNDARY: The case x = a is handled explicitly; the remainder is zero and the inequality holds. For n = 0 the factorial is 1! = 1 and ι(1) = 1_F > 0; the bound reduces to the mean-value inequality, which is correct. The factorial (n+1)! is a natural ≥1 for every n ∈ ℕ, so ι((n+1)!) is positive via lem‑of‑naturals‑positive, and division does not reverse inequalities. Absolute value properties needed for the product and reciprocal are standard consequences of lem‑of‑abs‑value and the ordered‑field arithmetic; the proof implicitly trusts them, a gap a competent reader closes immediately. No degenerate or empty cases affect the claim.\n\nSOURCES: All five supplied items—cor‑taylor‑lagrange‑and‑cauchy‑remainders, lem‑of‑abs‑value, def‑factorial‑and‑falling‑factorial, def‑canonical‑natural, lem‑of‑naturals‑positive—were inspected in their exact current text. The target’s proof uses only the Lagrange part of the first and the positivity/factorial facts from the others, and the matches are exact.\n\nCHECKED: Title, public statement, both numbered proof steps (1.1, 2.1), and the Facts & Assumptions were reviewed. The item has no Remarks. Every load‑bearing inference was probed; none is invalid.\n```"
