research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1305078-+{"id":"thm-lhopital-infinity-over-infinity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~kouba/CalcOneDIRECTORY/lhopitaldirectory/LHopital.html","https://math.colgate.edu/math323/dlantz/extras/notesC5.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the infinity-over-infinity rule for finite and infinite endpoints. The item consolidates endpoint modes, extended-real derivative limits, absolute divergence, and eventual fixed signs in the library's conventions. Its Cauchy-mean-value proof is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1305079-+{"id":"def-taylor-polynomial-and-remainder","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_taylor.html"],"rationale":"The source defines the degree-n Taylor polynomial and pointwise remainder with the same coefficients. The item adapts it to the library's canonical-natural and finite-sum notation and explicitly permits any point where the required derivatives exist.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
